EmbeddedProjectiveVariety ++ EmbeddedProjectiveVariety -- join of projective varieties
**************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ++: (Macaulay2Doc)++,
  * Usage: 
        X ++ Y
  * Inputs:
      * X, an *note embedded projective variety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,
      * Y, an *note embedded projective variety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, in
        the same ambient projective space of $X$
  * Outputs:
      * an *note embedded projective variety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, the
        join of $X$ and $Y$, that is, the closure of the union of lines of the
        form $\langle p,q\rangle$, with $p\in X$, $q\in Y$, and $p\neq q$

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K = ZZ/333331;                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = PP_K^(1,5); -- rational normal quintic curve                |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^5                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L = linearSpan {point ambient C,point ambient C}; -- random line|
|                                                                     |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^5                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C ++ L                                                          |
|                                                                     |
|o4 = threefold in PP^5 cut out by 5 hypersurfaces of degrees 3^4 4^1 |
|                                                                     |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety, threefold in PP^5                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C ++ C                                                          |
|                                                                     |
|o5 = threefold in PP^5 cut out by 4 hypersurfaces of degree 3        |
|                                                                     |
|o5 : ProjectiveVariety, threefold in PP^5                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : (point C) ++ (point C) ++ (point C)                             |
