EmbeddedProjectiveVariety ===> EmbeddedProjectiveVariety -- try to find an isomorphism between two projective varieties
***********************************************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ===>: (Macaulay2Doc)===>,
  * Usage: 
        X ===> Y
        Y <=== X
  * Inputs:
      * X, an *note embedded projective variety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,
      * Y, an *note embedded projective variety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,,
        projectively equivalent to X
  * Outputs:
      * a *note multi-rational map: MultirationalMap,, an isomorphism of the
        ambient spaces that sends X to Y (or an error if it fails)

Description
===========

This recursively tries to find an isomorphism between the base loci of the
*note parameterizations: parametrize_lpMultiprojectiveVariety_rp,.

In the following example, $X$ and $Y$ are two random rational normal curves of
degree 6 in $\mathbb{P}^6\subset\mathbb{P}^8$, and $V$ (resp., $W$) is a random
complete intersection of type (2,1) containing $X$ (resp., $Y$).

