Fano(ZZ,EmbeddedProjectiveVariety) -- Fano scheme of a projective variety
*************************************************************************

  * Function: *note Fano: (Macaulay2Doc)Fano,
  * Usage: 
        Fano(k,X)
        Fano(k,X,AffineChartGrass=>...)
        Fano X
        Fano(X,AffineChartGrass=>...)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, optional with default value
        equal to $\mathrm{dim}(X)$
      * X, an *note embedded projective variety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note embedded projective variety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, the
        subvariety of the *note Grassmannian: GrassmannianVariety,
        $\mathbb{G}(k,\mathrm{ambient}(X))$ that parametrizes the $k$-planes
        lying on $X$

Description
===========

This function is based internally on the function *note plucker:
(Resultants)plucker,, provided by the package *note Resultants:
(Resultants)Top,. In particular, note that by default the computation is done
on a randomly chosen affine chart on the Grassmannian. To change this behavior,
you can use the *note AffineChartGrass: (Resultants)AffineChartGrass, option.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K = ZZ/33331;                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = linearSpan {point PP_K^4,point PP_K^4}; -- a line in P^4            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^4                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : p := Fano L                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = point of coordinates [12627, 14941, 11188, -4847, 15437, 16492,         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety, a point in PP^9 (subvariety of codimension 6         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|13501, 8759, 6817, 1]                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|in GG(1,4) ⊂ PP^9)                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Fano p                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = curve in PP^4 cut out by 3 hypersurfaces of degree 1                    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^4                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(Fano p == L)                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If the input is a *note subvariety: MultiprojectiveVariety %
MultiprojectiveVariety, $Y\subset\mathbb{G}(k,\mathbb{P}^n)$, then the output
is the variety $W\subset\mathbb{P}^n$ swept out by the linear spaces
corresponding to points of $Y$. As an example, we now compute a surface scroll
$W\subset\mathbb{P}^4$ over an elliptic curve
$Y\subset\mathbb{G}(1,\mathbb{P}^4)$.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : G = GG_K(1,4);                                                       |
|                                                                          |
|o6 : ProjectiveVariety, GG(1,4)                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Y := (G * random({{1},{1},{1},{1},{1}},0_G)) % G -- an elliptic curve|
|                                                                          |
|o7 = curve in PP^9 cut out by 10 hypersurfaces of degrees 1^5 2^5         |
|                                                                          |
|o7 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^9 (subvariety of codimension 5 in G)  |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : W = Fano Y; -- surface swept out by the lines of Y                   |
|                                                                          |
|o8 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^4                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We can recover the subvariety $Y\subset\mathbb{G}(k,\mathbb{P}^n)$ by computing
the Fano variety of $k$-planes contained in $W$.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : Fano(1,W) -- variety of lines contained in W                       |
|                                                                        |
|o9 = curve in PP^9 cut out by 10 hypersurfaces of degrees 1^5 2^5       |
|                                                                        |
|o9 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^9 (subvariety of codimension 5 in G)|
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert(oo == Y)                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note plucker(Ideal): (Resultants)plucker, -- get the Plücker coordinates
    of a linear subspace
  * *note Fano(ZZ,Ideal): (Macaulay2Doc)Fano, -- compute the ideal of a Fano
    scheme in the Grassmannian
  * *note MultiprojectiveVariety % MultiprojectiveVariety:
    MultiprojectiveVariety % MultiprojectiveVariety, -- subvariety of a
    projective variety

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "Fano(EmbeddedProjectiveVariety)"
  * *note Fano(ZZ,EmbeddedProjectiveVariety):
    Fano_lpZZ_cmEmbeddedProjectiveVariety_rp, -- Fano scheme of a projective
    variety
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

