forceImage(MultirationalMap,MultiprojectiveVariety) -- declare which is the image of a multi-rational map
*********************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note forceImage: (Cremona)forceImage,
  * Usage: 
        forceImage(Phi,Y)
  * Inputs:
      * Phi, a *note multi-rational map: MultirationalMap,
      * Y, a *note multi-projective variety: MultiprojectiveVariety,
  * Outputs:
      * *note null: (Macaulay2Doc)null,

Description
===========

This method allows to inform the system about the image of a given
multi-rational map without performing any computation. In particular, this can
be used to declare that a rational map is dominant.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Phi = rationalMap {minors(3,(PP_(ZZ/65521)([6],2)).matrix)};            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : MultirationalMap (rational map from PP^6 to PP^9)                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Y = image(Phi,2)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Y                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, 6-dimensional subvariety of PP^9                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : forceImage(Phi,Y)                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : image Phi                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = Y                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety, 6-dimensional subvariety of PP^9                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Psi = rationalMap({minors(3,(PP_(ZZ/65521)([6],2)).matrix)},Dominant=>2 |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : MultirationalMap (rational map from PP^6 to 6-dimensional subvariety of |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|);                                                                           |
|                                                                             |
| PP^9)                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : forceImage(Psi,target Psi)                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Psi;                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : MultirationalMap (dominant rational map from PP^6 to 6-dimensional      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|subvariety of PP^9)                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

If the declaration is false, nonsensical answers may result.

See also
========

  * *note image(MultirationalMap): image_lpMultirationalMap_rp, -- image of a
    multi-rational map
  * *note forceImage(RationalMap,Ideal): (Cremona)forceImage, -- declare which
    is the image of a rational map

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note forceImage(MultirationalMap,MultiprojectiveVariety):
    forceImage_lpMultirationalMap_cmMultiprojectiveVariety_rp, -- declare which
    is the image of a multi-rational map
  * "forceImage(MultirationalMap,ZZ)"
