Hom(MultiprojectiveVariety,MultiprojectiveVariety) -- get the hom-set of rational maps between two multi-projective varieties
*****************************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note Hom: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom,
  * Usage: 
        Hom(X,Y)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note multi-projective variety: MultiprojectiveVariety,
      * Y, a *note multi-projective variety: MultiprojectiveVariety,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DegreeLimit: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note MinimalGenerators: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value true,
      * *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hom-set: RAT,, the hom-set of *note rational maps:
        MultirationalMap, from X to Y

Description
===========

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K = ZZ/3;                                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = random({1,1},0_(PP_K^{1,1}));                                      |
|                                                                            |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^1 x PP^1                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Y = PP_K^{2,1,3};                                                      |
|                                                                            |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety, PP^2 x PP^1 x PP^3                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Hom(X,Y)                                                               |
|                                                                            |
|o4 = Hom-set of rational maps                                               |
|     from curve in PP^1 x PP^1 defined by a multi-form of multi-degree (1,1)|
|     to PP^2 x PP^1 x PP^3                                                  |
|                                                                            |
|o4 : Hom(X,Y)                                                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Some or all of the arguments may be omitted.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Hom(X,)                                                                |
|                                                                            |
