inverse(MultirationalMap) -- inverse of a birational map
********************************************************

  * Function: *note inverse: (Macaulay2Doc)inverse,
  * Usage: 
        inverse Phi
        Phi^-1
        inverse(Phi,Verify=>true)
        inverse(Phi,Verify=>false)
  * Inputs:
      * Phi, a *note multi-rational map: MultirationalMap,, a birational map
  * Outputs:
      * a *note multi-rational map: MultirationalMap,, the inverse map of Phi

Description
===========

This function applies a general algorithm to calculate the inverse map passing
through the computation of the *note graph: graph_lpMultirationalMap_rp,. Note
that by default the option Verify is set to true, which means that the
birationality of the map is verified using *note degree:
degree_lpMultirationalMap_rp, Phi == 1 and *note image:
image_lpMultirationalMap_rp, Phi == *note target: target_lpMultirationalMap_rp,
Phi.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : -- map defined by the quadrics through a rational normal quartic curve  |
|     Phi = rationalMap PP_(ZZ/65521)^(1,4);                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : MultirationalMap (rational map from PP^4 to PP^5)                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : -- we see Phi as a dominant map                                         |
|     Phi = rationalMap(Phi,image Phi);                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : MultirationalMap (dominant rational map from PP^4 to hypersurface in    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|PP^5)                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : time inverse Phi;                                                       |
| -- used 0.134544s (cpu); 0.0941464s (thread); 0s (gc)                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : MultirationalMap (birational map from hypersurface in PP^5 to PP^4)     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Psi = last graph Phi;                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : MultirationalMap (birational map from 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^4 x|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|PP^5 to hypersurface in PP^5)                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : time inverse Psi;                                                       |
| -- used 0.166457s (cpu); 0.115171s (thread); 0s (gc)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : MultirationalMap (birational map from hypersurface in PP^5 to           |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|4-dimensional subvariety of PP^4 x PP^5)                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Eta = first graph Psi;                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : MultirationalMap (birational map from 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^4 x|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|PP^5 x PP^5 to 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^4 x PP^5)                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : time inverse Eta;                                                       |
| -- used 0.474214s (cpu); 0.397203s (thread); 0s (gc)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : MultirationalMap (birational map from 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^4 x|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|PP^5 to 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^4 x PP^5 x PP^5)                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert(Phi * Phi^-1 == 1 and Phi^-1 * Phi == 1)                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert(Psi * Psi^-1 == 1 and Psi^-1 * Psi == 1)                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert(Eta * Eta^-1 == 1 and Eta^-1 * Eta == 1)                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

References
==========

ArXiv preprint: Computations with rational maps between multi-projective
varieties (see https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.04503 ).

Caveat
======

If the option Verify is set to false (which is preferable for efficiency), then
no test is done to check that the map is birational, and if not then often the
error is not thrown at all and a nonsense answer is returned.

