inverse2 -- inverse of a birational map using a faster algorithm for a special class of maps
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        inverse2 Phi
        inverse2(Phi,Verify=>true)
        inverse2(Phi,Verify=>false)
  * Inputs:
      * Phi, a *note multi-rational map: MultirationalMap,, a birational map of
        so-called multi-linear type
  * Outputs:
      * a *note multi-rational map: MultirationalMap,, the inverse map of Phi

Description
===========

This assumes that the *note graph: graph_lpMultirationalMap_rp, of the input
map Phi is defined by a simplified system of equations, which may not be true.
If the option Verify is set to true, which is the default choice, then it is
verified that the left and right composition of Phi with the returned map is
the identity, throwing an error if this is not the case.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K = ZZ/10000019;                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : -- map defined by the cubics through the secant variety to the rational |
|     Phi = multirationalMap rationalMap(ring PP_K^6,ring GG_K(2,4),gens ideal|
|                                                                             |
|o2 : MultirationalMap (rational map from PP^6 to GG(2,4))                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|normal curve of degree 6                                                     |
| PP_K([6],2));                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : time Psi = inverse2 Phi;                                                |
| -- used 0.416296s (cpu); 0.381572s (thread); 0s (gc)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : MultirationalMap (birational map from GG(2,4) to PP^6)                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert(Phi * Psi == 1)                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Phi' = Phi || Phi;                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : MultirationalMap (rational map from PP^6 x PP^6 to GG(2,4) x GG(2,4))   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : time Psi' = inverse2 Phi';                                              |
| -- used 1.74361s (cpu); 1.36093s (thread); 0s (gc)                          |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : MultirationalMap (birational map from GG(2,4) x GG(2,4) to PP^6 x PP^6) |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(Phi' * Psi' == 1)                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note inverse(MultirationalMap): inverse_lpMultirationalMap_rp, -- inverse
    of a birational map
  * *note MultirationalMap <==> MultirationalMap: MultirationalMap <==>
    MultirationalMap, -- equality of multi-rational maps with checks on
    internal data

Ways to use inverse2:
=====================

  * "inverse2(MultirationalMap)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note inverse2: inverse2, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

