rationalMap(MultiprojectiveVariety,Tally) -- rational map defined by an effective divisor
*****************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note rationalMap: (Cremona)rationalMap,
  * Usage: 
        rationalMap(X,D)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note multi-projective variety: MultiprojectiveVariety,
      * D, a *note tally: (Macaulay2Doc)Tally,, a multiset of pure codimension
        1 *note subschemes: MultiprojectiveVariety % MultiprojectiveVariety, of
        $X$ with no embedded components; so that D is interpreted as an
        effective divisor on $X$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Dominant: (Cremona)Dominant, => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note multi-rational map: MultirationalMap,, the rational map defined
        by the complete linear system $|D|$

Description
===========

In the example below, we take a smooth complete intersection
$X\subset\mathbb{P}^5$ of three quadrics containing a conic
$C\subset\mathbb{P}^5$. Then we calculate the map defined by the linear system
$|2H+C|$, where $H$ is the hyperplane section class of $X$.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P5 = PP_(ZZ/65521)^5;                            |
|                                                      |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety, PP^5                          |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = random({{2},3:{1}},0_P5);                    |
|                                                      |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^5                 |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = random({3:{2}},C);                           |
|                                                      |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^5               |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : H = random(1,0_X); -- it's interpreted as X * H  |
|                                                      |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety, hypersurface in PP^5          |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = tally {H, H, C}                              |
|                                                      |
|o5 = Tally{C => 1}                                    |
|           H => 2                                     |
|                                                      |
|o5 : Tally                                            |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : phi = rationalMap(X,D)                           |
|                                                      |
|o6 = phi                                              |
|                                                      |
|o6 : MultirationalMap (rational map from X to PP^20)  |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(phi == rationalMap(X,tally {X*H, X*H, C}))|
+------------------------------------------------------+

This function is based internally on the function *note
rationalMap(Ring,Tally): (Cremona)rationalMap_lpRing_cmTally_rp,, provided by
the package *note Cremona: (Cremona)Top,.

See also
========

  * *note rationalMap(Ring,Tally): (Cremona)rationalMap_lpRing_cmTally_rp, --
    rational map defined by an effective divisor

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "rationalMap(EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,Tally,ZZ)"
