===========

Weighted projective varieties can be constructed using the function *note
projectiveVariety: projectiveVariety,, just like multi- and embedded projective
varieties.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[u,v,w,x,y,z,Degrees=>{{2},{1},{3},{1},{7},{5}}]/ideal((3/2)*u+6*v|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|^2+v*x+4*x^2,(3/2)*u*v+(4/5)*v^3+w+(3/2)*u*x+(3/7)*v^2*x+3*v*x^2+(5/6)*x^3); |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : projectiveVariety R                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = threefold in PP(2,1,3,1,7,5) cut out by 2 hypersurfaces of degrees 2^1  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, threefold in PP(2,1,3,1,7,5)                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3^1                                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : describe oo                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = ambient:.............. PP(2,1,3,1,7,5)                                  |
|     dim:.................. 3                                                |
|     codim:................ 2                                                |
|     degree:............... 6                                                |
|     generators:........... 2^1 3^1                                          |
|     purity:............... true                                             |
|     dim sing. l.:......... -1                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Here is a shortcut to construct weighted projective spaces:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = ZZ/65521;                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : PP_K(2,1,3,1,7,5)                                                       |
|warning: clearing value of symbol x to allow access to subscripted           |
|       : debug with expression   debug 9868   or with command line           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = PP(2,1,3,1,7,5)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : ProjectiveVariety, PP(2,1,3,1,7,5)                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|variables based on it                                                        |
|option   --debug 9868                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This class is currently experimental and under development.

See also
========

  * *note WeightedRationalMap: WeightedRationalMap, -- the class of all
    weighted-rational maps
  * *note MultiprojectiveVariety: MultiprojectiveVariety, -- the class of all
    multi-projective varieties
  * *note EmbeddedProjectiveVariety: EmbeddedProjectiveVariety, -- the class of
    all embedded projective varieties

For the programmer
==================

The object *note WeightedProjectiveVariety: WeightedProjectiveVariety, is a
*note type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note
MultiprojectiveVariety: MultiprojectiveVariety, < *note MutableHashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, < *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, <
*note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

